<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::mil_escalation_level" target="global_energy_supply_sho::diesel_export_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher kinetic escalation causes damage to refineries, terminals and export infrastructure and prompts port closures and insurer/charterer refusals, directly reducing volumes of diesel shipped out of the region.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">global_energy_supply_sho</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::mil_escalation_level" target="iran_middle_east_tension::shipping_security_risk" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">A marked uptick in Russian military escalation draws NATO and allied naval assets and intelligence focus toward European waters and increases risk of wider naval confrontation, reducing deterrence and leaving Middle East shipping lanes more exposed to interdiction and attacks.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_middle_east_tension</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::mil_escalation_level" target="sovereign_bond_market_st::volatility_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">A sudden uptick in kinetic operations raises near‑term geopolitical uncertainty and tail‑risk concerns, triggering rapid hedging and repricing across sovereign bonds and raising both realized and implied market volatility.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">sovereign_bond_market_st</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::mil_escalation_level" target="us_china_tech_trade_riva::systemic_safety_risk" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher kinetic and hybrid escalation incentivizes rushed deployment and operationalization of autonomous, cyber, and decision‑support AI systems with compressed testing and oversight, raising the aggregate probability of unsafe or cascading AI failures.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_trade_riva</data>
</edge>
