<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_pressure" target="global_energy_supply_sho::diesel_spot_price_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">Broader or stricter sanctions on Russian refined products, payment/insurance channels and trading entities removes accessible supply and raises transaction frictions and risk premia, directly pushing up global diesel spot prices.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">global_energy_supply_sho</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_pressure" target="iran_middle_east_tension::crude_export_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Tightening and enforcement of sanctions on Russian oil creates supply gaps and pricing incentives that prompt buyers and middlemen to source additional crude from Iran via sanctioned or opaque commercial channels, raising Iran's effective export volumes.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_middle_east_tension</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_pressure" target="sovereign_bond_market_st::nominal_yield_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Broader or more severe sanctions that implicate banks, payment channels or commodity flows increase counterparty and sovereign risk premia (and term premia) in affected jurisdictions, pushing up long‑term government bond yields.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">sovereign_bond_market_st</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_pressure" target="us_china_tech_trade_riva::compute_capacity_total" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Broader sanctions and export controls tied to the conflict restrict shipments of advanced accelerators, chip fabrication equipment, and design tools, directly reducing the volume of new high‑end compute hardware that adversary states and firms can acquire and deploy.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_trade_riva</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::corp_withdrawal_flow" target="russia_ukraine_war::energy_resilience" id="0">
  <data key="d28">intra_causal</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::corp_withdrawal_flow" target="russia_ukraine_war::investment_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">intra_causal</data>
