<edge source="iran_middle_east_tension::military_incident_rate" target="russia_ukraine_war::defense_aid_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">A spike in concentrated Middle East military incidents forces the US and NATO to reallocate limited stockpiles, transport capacity and urgent procurement priorities to the region, reducing the quantity and speed of materiel that can be diverted to Ukraine.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_middle_east_tension</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_middle_east_tension::military_incident_rate" target="russia_ukraine_war::diplomatic_cooperation" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">High-intensity incidents in the Middle East consume diplomatic bandwidth and political attention among Western capitals, undermining unity and the capacity for coordinated multilateral action on Russia/Ukraine issues.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_middle_east_tension</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_middle_east_tension::military_incident_rate" target="sovereign_bond_market_st::volatility_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">Sudden upticks in military incidents generate news-driven re-pricing and order-flow imbalances that produce spikes in realized and implied volatility in sovereign bond markets.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_middle_east_tension</data>
  <data key="d40">sovereign_bond_market_st</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_middle_east_tension::military_incident_rate" target="us_china_tech_trade_riva::regulatory_enforcement" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Heightened military incidents increase political pressure in the US, EU and allied capitals to expand and more aggressively enforce export controls, sanctions and review of tech transfers related to semiconductors and AI, producing measurable increases in enforcement actions and scrutiny.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_middle_east_tension</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_trade_riva</data>
