<edge source="iran_middle_east_tension::crude_export_flow" target="global_energy_supply_sho::diesel_export_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">A drop in regional crude exports reduces feedstock availability for nearby refineries (or forces them to run on more expensive alternatives), lowering refinery throughput and thus net diesel available for export from those refining hubs.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_middle_east_tension</data>
  <data key="d40">global_energy_supply_sho</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_middle_east_tension::crude_export_flow" target="russia_ukraine_war::energy_resilience" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">A sharp reduction in Middle East crude exports tightens global spare capacity and limits replacement options for cut Russian supplies, lowering the practical ability of Ukraine and its partners to absorb energy disruptions.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_middle_east_tension</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_middle_east_tension::crude_export_flow" target="us_china_tech_trade_riva::capital_inflow_ai" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">A sustained drop in regional crude export volumes reduces sovereign and oil‑sector cashflows and shortens liquidity windows for regional sovereign wealth funds and energy investors, leading them to scale back allocations to overseas AI startups and infrastructure financing.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_middle_east_tension</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_trade_riva</data>
</edge>
