  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising developed‑market nominal yields raise global discount rates and tend to strengthen the dollar and increase financing costs for commodity inventory/hedging, which suppresses demand and pushes down spot crude prices within months.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">sovereign_bond_market_st</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_middle_east_tension</data>
