  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">A drop in bond market liquidity forces energy firms and utilities to pay higher short‑term funding and hedging costs or face margin calls, reducing inventory financing and investment in redundancy and thereby degrading near‑term energy supply resilience.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">sovereign_bond_market_st</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
